JSX.ElementとかReact.ReactNodeのどっちがいいかとかが分かっていないです","ts":"1635913738.292700","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"S3SuL"}]},{"client_msg_id":"fe120968-2557-4682-bf70-c412712626d3","type":"message","user":"U8996GYBF","text":"それなら一括置換でいけますね","ts":"1635913719.292300","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"nE3oU"}]},{"client_msg_id":"394547bc-f7ff-428f-ae9f-52a8cd695c50","type":"message","user":"U78A6ESHM","text":"children が必要なら VFC に `children: React.ReactNode` と書いておいて、18 がリリースされたら VFC を FC に変えてあげれば移行完了か。","ts":"1635913704.292100","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"=10M8"}]},{"client_msg_id":"1e08e8b3-70f1-462a-85a5-9edc66c46d75","type":"message","user":"U8996GYBF","text":"FC\u0026lt;Props\u0026gt; or (props: Props) は宗教感がある","ts":"1635913640.291400","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"Ev+"}]},{"client_msg_id":"97361736-36c7-415e-8a2f-41cee27f5496","type":"message","user":"U78A6ESHM","text":"ですね。","ts":"1635913573.290300","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"jgds"}]},{"client_msg_id":"fd711508-2fa8-4e9a-8ccf-a9a9a2f1dce7","type":"message","user":"U8996GYBF","text":"breaking changeだけどまぁchildren書けばいいだけだから修正可能な範囲ですよね","ts":"1635913550.290100","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"qremA"}]},{"client_msg_id":"6fb9e77f-84e4-471f-b80d-742780ef1b12","type":"message","user":"U78A6ESHM","text":"18 からかな。\n\u003chttps://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/issues/46691\u003e","ts":"1635913497.289300","attachments":[{"color":"36a64f","fallback":"\u003chttps://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/issues/46691|#46691 [RFC] React 18 and types-only breaking changes\u003e","id":1,"title":"\u003chttps://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/issues/46691|#46691 [RFC] React 18 and types-only breaking changes\u003e","text":"Edit: We're likely not doing that in 17 but 18 to make the 17 upgrade as easy as possible. See \u003chttps://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/issues/46691#issuecomment-672840456|#46691 (comment)\u003e for more context.\n\nAmong active contributors we talked informally about making some breaking changes to `@types/react` in an upcoming major release of React that we think will improve the typings long-term. Now that a \u003chttps://reactjs.org/blog/2020/08/10/react-v17-rc.html|release candidate for React 17\u003e is available we should formalize what breaking changes we want to make.\n\nGitHub issues is not the best place for discussing umbrella topics (no threading) but hopefully this will do.\n\n*breaking changes*\n\n• remove `@deprecated` types  \n    These can be flagged in `tslint`\n    ☐ `ReactType` (\u003chttps://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/pull/56049|#56049\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/pull/56396|#56396\u003e)\n    ☑︎ `SFCElement` (\u003chttps://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/pull/56397|#56397\u003e)\n    ☑︎ `SFCFactory` (currently no usage in published `@types/` packages)\n    ☐ `SFC` (\u003chttps://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/pull/56052|#56052\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/pull/56402|#56402\u003e)\n    ☐ `StatelessComponent` (\u003chttps://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/pull/56399|#56399\u003e)\n    ☑︎ `RefForwardingComponent` (Accidental usage removed in \u003chttps://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/pull/56414|#56414\u003e which shows how the old name looks right but is most likely misused)\n    ☐ `Props` (\u003chttps://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/pull/56416|#56416\u003e)\n• remove implicitly typed `children` from `React.FC` (and the corresponding overload of `React.memo`)  \n    In TypeScript it's generally easier to add types than remove them.  \n    Closes \u003chttps://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/issues/33006|#33006\u003e  \n    Closes \u003chttps://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/issues/34237|#34237\u003e\n• Require TypeScript 3.?  \n    Depending on the time frame we should align with the default \u003chttps://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped#older-versions-of-typescript-29-and-earlier|supported version in DefinitelTyped\u003e. From the usage stats in VSCode these older TypeScript versions are rarely used.  \n    Using TypeScript 3.x would allow us to replace `any` with `unknown` which is probably the change with the biggest impact.\n    • \u003chttps://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/issues/52873|#52873\u003e\n• ~Remove `event.persist()`?~\n    • \u003chttps://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/issues/46691#issuecomment-672839026|#46691 (comment)\u003e\n☐ Remove `{}` from `ReactFragment` (\u003chttps://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/pull/56026|#56026\u003e)\n\n\u003chttps://github.com/gaearon|@gaearon\u003e Should we hold off with removing deprecated React features? We currently flag the following features as deprecated:\n\n• deprecated lifecycles (cWM, cWRP, cWU, `UNSAFE_` prefixed lifecycles)  \n    Maybe removing the unprefixed ones is a viable migration path?\n• class component constructors with context as the second argument\n• class components `this.refs` i.e. string refs\n\n*features*\n\nAlready part of `next.d.ts`\n\n*How to go about it?*\n\nSee \u003chttps://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/pull/46690|#46690\u003e where we can test the approaches. Ideally `@types` would understand pre-releases but I couldn't find documentation about it so we have to be practical about the approach chosen.\n\n*`@types/react` authors*\n\n\u003chttps://github.com/johnnyreilly|@johnnyreilly\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/bbenezech|@bbenezech\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/pzavolinsky|@pzavolinsky\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/digiguru|@digiguru\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/ericanderson|@ericanderson\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/DovydasNavickas|@DovydasNavickas\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/theruther4d|@theruther4d\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/guilhermehubner|@guilhermehubner\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/ferdaber|@ferdaber\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/jrakotoharisoa|@jrakotoharisoa\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/pascaloliv|@pascaloliv\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/Hotell|@Hotell\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/franklixuefei|@franklixuefei\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/Jessidhia|@Jessidhia\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/saranshkataria|@saranshkataria\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/lukyth|@lukyth\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/eps1lon|@eps1lon\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/zieka|@zieka\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/dancerphil|@dancerphil\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/dimitropoulos|@dimitropoulos\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/disjukr|@disjukr\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/vhfmag|@vhfmag\u003e, \u003chttps://github.com/hellatan|@hellatan\u003e","fields":[{"title":"Comments","value":"23","short":true}],"mrkdwn_in":["text"],"blocks":null,"footer":"\u003chttps://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped|DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped\u003e","footer_icon":"https://slack.github.com/static/img/favicon-neutral.png","ts":1597233118}],"team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"423HE"}]},{"client_msg_id":"39397cea-48f4-4cd1-ad65-b35766018ec3","type":"message","user":"U9S4G0LJW","text":"なるほど","ts":"1635913433.289000","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"ft7kD"}]},{"client_msg_id":"0f478cae-c865-49ba-b573-aa6f5f6f2fc1","type":"message","user":"U8996GYBF","text":"バージョンいくつか忘れたけどFCにchildrenが入らなくなってほぼ等価になるはず","ts":"1